---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: false
scene: true
description: "LRACDIMENSION is the engineering environment of John Carl Dimatulac: web systems, automation, and the tools behind them, organised into five working dimensions."
---
<section class="studio-hero shell">
<div class="studio-copy"><p class="overline">{{ site.name }} / Engineering environment</p><h1>Web systems.<br>Automation.<br><span>Engineering.</span></h1><p class="studio-intro">I design and build digital systems that solve real operational problems: websites and business applications, automation, and the data tools behind them. This site is organised as five working dimensions, and you can use them.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn" href="/vector/">Website diagnostic ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/work/">View work ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="#dimensions">Explore the dimensions ↗</a></div></div>
<div class="system-stage" data-system-stage><div class="system-viewport" data-system-canvas aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="system-fallback" data-system-fallback aria-hidden="true"><span>INTERFACE</span><span>API</span><span>AUTOMATION</span><span>DATA</span></div><div class="scene-toolbar"><span>Inside the system</span><button type="button" class="motion-toggle" data-motion-toggle hidden aria-pressed="false">Pause motion</button></div><div class="layer-controls" role="group" aria-label="Explore the system layers"><button type="button" data-layer="0" aria-pressed="true">Interface</button><button type="button" data-layer="1" aria-pressed="false">API</button><button type="button" data-layer="2" aria-pressed="false">Automation</button><button type="button" data-layer="3" aria-pressed="false">Data</button></div><p class="layer-description" data-layer-description aria-live="polite">Interfaces people use. React, Next.js, and WordPress.</p></div>
</section>

<section class="portfolio-section shell" id="dimensions"><div class="section-title"><p class="overline">Explore dimensions</p><h2>Five environments.<br>One system.</h2><p>Each dimension is a capability area with something you can open, read, or run. Together they are the evidence for what I build.</p></div>
<ol class="dim-grid" aria-label="Dimensions">{% for d in dimensions %}<li class="dim-card" data-status="{{ d.status }}" data-enter><a href="{{ d.href }}" class="dim-card__link"><span class="dim-card__index">{{ d.index }}</span><span class="dim-card__name">{{ d.name | upper }}</span><span class="dim-card__descriptor">{{ d.descriptor }}</span><span class="dim-card__summary">{{ d.summary }}</span><span class="dim-card__verbs">{% for v in d.verbs %}{{ v }}{% if not loop.last %} → {% endif %}{% endfor %}</span><span class="dim-card__foot"><span class="dim-card__proves">Proves: {{ d.proves }}</span>{% if d.status == 'building' %}<span class="dim-status dim-status--building"><span></span>In build</span>{% else %}<span class="dim-status"><span></span>Live</span>{% endif %}</span></a></li>{% endfor %}</ol></section>

<section class="portfolio-section shell" id="selected-work"><div class="section-title"><p class="overline">01 / Work</p><h2>Selected work.</h2><p>Three of fifteen. Client work, a working demo, and an independent concept, each with a real screenshot and a case study that states the problem, the architecture, and what shipped.</p></div><div class="project-showcase">{% for project in portfolio | slice_first(3) %}<article class="project-feature" data-enter><a class="project-image" href="/work/{{ project.slug }}/" aria-label="Open {{ project.title }} case study"><img src="/assets/img/projects/{{ project.image }}.webp" width="{{ project.imageWidth }}" height="{{ project.imageHeight }}" alt="{{ project.title }} website homepage" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></a><div class="project-caption"><div><p class="project-type">{{ project.kind }} / {{ project.field }}</p><h3><a href="/work/{{ project.slug }}/">{{ project.title }} ↗</a></h3></div><p>{{ project.summary }}</p></div></article>{% endfor %}</div><a class="text-link" href="/work/">All {{ portfolio.length }} projects ↗</a></section>

<section class="portfolio-section shell capabilities" id="what-i-build"><div><p class="overline">What I build</p><h2>The interface.<br>The engine.<br><span>The connection.</span></h2><a class="text-link" href="/services/">Services in detail ↗</a></div><div class="capability-list"><article><h3>Websites and web applications</h3><p>React and TypeScript interfaces, WordPress platforms with custom plugins and REST integrations, connected to Node.js, PHP, and database-backed services.</p></article><article><h3>Business systems and automation</h3><p>Operations systems, message centres, learning platforms, and n8n pipelines that move work between the tools a team already uses.</p></article><article><h3>Engines and data tools</h3><p>The analysis, scoring, and monitoring layers behind those systems: the engines that run Vector and Signal on this site.</p></article></div></section>

<section class="pipeline-section" id="vector-featured"><div class="shell"><div class="section-title"><p class="overline">Featured system / 02 Vector</p><h2>Web Clinic.<br>Examine, diagnose, prescribe.</h2><p>Enter a public website. Seven analyzers read it, a documented scoring engine grades it, every issue carries its evidence, and the result is a prioritised prescription you can share by link and compare over time.</p></div><form class="vector-inline" action="/vector/" method="get" data-vector-inline><label for="home-vector-url" class="label">Website URL</label><div class="vector-inline__row"><input id="home-vector-url" name="url" type="text" inputmode="url" autocomplete="url" placeholder="company.com" required><button type="submit" class="btn">Examine ↗</button></div><p class="fine-print">Technical, SEO, performance indicators, accessibility, security headers, links, and content. Not Core Web Vitals and not a vulnerability scan; the report says exactly what it measured.</p></form></div></section>

<section class="portfolio-section shell" id="approach"><div class="section-title"><p class="overline">Engineering approach</p><h2>Diagnose first.<br>Build the smallest system that works.</h2></div><ol class="approach-list">{% for step in process %}<li data-enter><span class="project-type">{{ loop.index0 | pad }} / {{ step.duration }}</span><h3>{{ step.title }}</h3><p>{{ step.lede }}</p><p class="approach-list__output"><b>Output:</b> {{ step.output }}</p></li>{% endfor %}</ol><a class="text-link" href="/process/">The full process ↗</a></section>

<section class="portfolio-section shell" id="research"><div class="section-title"><p class="overline">05 / Research</p><h2>Notes from<br>the field.</h2><p>Sourced articles and build logs on AI, web development, and how systems are put together.</p></div><div class="research-strip">{% for post in collections.research | sort(false, false, "data.order") | slice_first(3) %}<article data-enter>{% if post.data.image %}<a class="note-thumb" href="{{ post.url }}" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="{{ post.data.image }}" alt="" width="1024" height="572" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></a>{% endif %}<p class="project-type">{{ post.data.topic }} / {{ post.templateContent | reading_time }} min read</p><h3><a href="{{ post.url }}">{{ post.data.title }}</a></h3><p>{{ post.data.description }}</p></article>{% endfor %}</div><a class="text-link" href="/research/">All research ↗</a></section>
{% include "partials/studio-contact.njk" %}
